1571 0 obj
<<
  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 1570 0 R
  /Alt (A three-panel controlled metric fixture. Panel A shows a reconstructed point and its exact closest point on a triangle. Panel B uses a solid arrow from a reconstructed point to its nearest triangle and a dashed arrow from a triangle to its nearest reconstructed point, distinguishing the two directional reductions. Panel C holds one planar surface and five points fixed while replacing four equal-area faces with a left-weighted non-uniform tessellation in which the left region contributes thirty-two of forty equal-weight faces. Accuracy remains 0.00640 square metres, while equal-face completeness changes from 0.03640 to 0.02284 square metres. The values are synthetic validity evidence, not an ASE result.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
  >>]
  /K [72]
  /Pg 5034 0 R
>>
